# 🎮 CORE GAME STRUCTURE

The game is divided into Acts:

ACT I — Greenest in Flames  
ACT II — Raider Camp & Hatchery  
ACT III — Northern Journey  
ACT IV — Naerytar / Lodge / Skyreach  
ACT V — Rise of Tiamat & Council

Each act must contain:
- Rooms
- Decision nodes
- Conditional options based on party presence
- Checkpoints
- Variables impacted
- Possible divergences

---

# 👥 GROUP SYSTEM

Mode A — Unified Group

The player controls the group as one entity.

Each character:
- Has skill tags
- Has narrative abilities
- Can be injured
- Can die permanently
- Can be absent
- Can be replaced later

Options appear conditionally:

[Option – Bjolnir: Redemption]
[Option – Malar: Stealth]
[Option – Darrin: Wild Magic]

If character not present → option not shown.

---

# ⚔️ RESOLUTION SYSTEM

No visible dice.

Resolution types:
- Success
- Success with cost
- Failure
- Critical failure
- Death

Combat is narrative-based, not mechanical RPG combat.

Duel with Cyanwrath must:
- Allow canonical defeat + survival.
- Allow alternative outcomes.
- Never force game over by default.

---

# 💀 GAME OVER SYSTEM

Two types:

1) Serious Game Over
- Narrative collapse
- Group death
- Strategic failure

2) Silly Game Over
- Humorous failure
- Overconfidence
- Absurd decision

After Game Over:
- Restore last checkpoint.
- Do NOT restart entire game.

---

# 🔁 CHECKPOINT SYSTEM

Each major decision creates a snapshot of:
- Characters states
- Flags
- Inventory
- Variables
- Act progression

Rollback must restore all of these.

---

# 📊 GLOBAL VARIABLES

Examples:
- Reputation_Civilians
- Reputation_Authorities
- Chaos_Level
- Group_Morale
- Political_Trust
- Dragon_Influence

These must influence later acts.

---

# 🎨 VISUAL DIRECTION

Pixel art, 32–48 color palette.
Deterministic animation.
No frame randomness.

320x200 internal resolution scaled.

---

# ✍️ WRITING STYLE

Language: French
Tone: Epic, immersive, serious
Dialogues: Short, character-driven
No modern slang
Silly Game Over allowed to include light irony

---

# 🧱 DATA-DRIVEN DESIGN

All narrative and branching content must be structured in objects:

- acts
- rooms
- characters
- flags
- variables
- decisions
- checkpoints

Do NOT hard-code branching inside UI code.

